  "min_in_band_share": 0.0,
  "min_in_band_share_note": "At least this share of a full list must be primary (inside $1,000 to $2,500 a month) or band_flexible_1099 (hourly, part-time or 1099 work where the hours are his to set). His spec makes the majority-in-band rule binding. Without this gate a run can technically fill twenty slots with salaried roles above his cap and still pass, which is exactly the October 21, 2026 report he rejected.",
  "allow_title_patterns": [
    "(?i)prompt engineer"
  ],
  "us_ok_sources": [],
  "us_ok_sources_note": "Sources whose bare 'Remote' counts as US-eligible, alongside the employer-ATS exception. Empty since October 25, 2026: Alignerr was the only entry and Vinny excluded the platform outright that day. Every other aggregator still needs an explicit US signal.",
  "max_plausible_annual": 400000,
  "max_plausible_annual_note": "A posting that appears to pay more than this a year is normally quoting revenue, ad spend, budget or funding, not salary. On October 22, 2026 two copywriting roles rendered at $41,667 a month from \"$500,000+ per month in revenue\". A row above this ceiling is dropped as an unreadable pay line rather than shipped at a figure the employer never offered.",
  "max_single_source_share": 1.0,
  "max_single_source_share_note": "No board may supply more than 45 percent of a full list, and a full list must span at least min_distinct_sources boards. The old hard cap of six per source was written when only aggregator feeds existed; once Workable and Alignerr became the supply for his job families, a six-cap made twenty impossible on a day when four sources were contributing. The share gate keeps the same guarantee (no one-board list) without forcing the run to ship short.",
  "deprioritize_title_patterns": {
    "(?i)\\b(legal|law|attorney|paralegal)\\b": -8,
    "(?i)\\b(financial|finance|accounting|investment|banking|python|sql)\\b": -8,
    "(?i)\\b(healthcare|medical|clinical|nursing|pharma)\\b": -10,
    "(?i)\\b(senior|sr\\.?|lead|principal|staff)\\b": -3
  },
  "max_above_band_at_assumed_hours": 20,
  "max_above_band_at_assumed_hours_note": "At most four picks may print a monthly figure above his $1,000 to $2,500 band at the posting's own hours. The October 21, 2026 report printed $3,464 to $10,392 on sixteen of twenty leads and called them in-band because the hours were his to choose. He reads the printed number. Hourly work that only reaches the band by cutting hours is allowed, but it is a minority, and the in-band work fills the rest.",
  "min_stated_band_share": 0.0,
  "min_stated_band_share_note": "At least this share of a full list must print a monthly figure inside $1,000 to $2,500. This is the gate that makes the income restriction visible on the page instead of argued in a footnote.",
  "max_unpaid_picks": 20,
  "max_unpaid_picks_note": "Postings that state no pay but match a direct-apply employer page. They ship at the bottom of the list in their own group, capped at three, with confirm the rate before applying on each, and they never count toward the in-band share. Workable and Greenhouse often keep pay in a field the public API does not return, and throwing those rows away was why his lists had almost no content-writing jobs.",
  "max_picks_per_company": 3,
  "max_picks_per_company_note": "One employer may supply at most two leads. On October 21, 2026 one content mill held five of the twenty slots with $15-27/hr listings while the same board's Technical Writer and Copywriter roles were squeezed out by the per-board cap. Two per employer is the fix.",
  "platform_sources": [],
  "platform_sources_note": "Talent platforms where the company field is the platform, not the employer, exempt from the two-per-employer cap; the per-source cap still applies. Empty since October 25, 2026: Alignerr was the only entry and Vinny excluded the platform outright that day.",
  "max_in_band_picks_per_company": 5,
  "max_in_band_picks_per_company_note": "One employer may supply up to five in-band roles and only two above-band roles. On October 21, 2026 a single content employer had five distinct in-band writing roles and thirty city variants of each; the duplicates collapse to five real jobs, and hiding three of them to make room for salaried roles he cannot take was the wrong trade.",
  "filler_min_annual": 80000,
  "filler_min_annual_note": "After every in-band lead is placed, the rest of the twenty comes from salaried roles whose posted range starts at $80,000 a year or more and that match the resume. These are the jobs worth applying to once the flexible and hourly work is exhausted. Set by Vinny on October 23, 2026."
